N-Body Simulation
===============================================================================
section: Examples
+> combinatorics
+> stats
===============================================================================

This program integrates the mutual gravitational interaction of the Sun, eight
planets, and Pluto. Every body influences every other body; the visualization is
a projection of the live simulated state, not a collection of prescribed
orbits.


1. Initial Conditions
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Positions use astronomical units, velocities use astronomical units per year,
and masses are normalized so the gravitational constant is one. As in the
Computer Language Benchmarks Game reference system, the Sun's initial velocity
cancels the planets' total momentum. Mercury's heliocentric ecliptic state is a
JPL Horizons vector for 1974-06-04; unlike the previously copied velocity, it
has the planet's independently published semimajor axis and eccentricity.

@clock := timer://clock/tick{:read(tick)}
@scene := scene://orbit/frame{:write(replace)}

  days-per-year := 365.24
  π := 3.141592654
  solar-mass := 4 * π ^ 2
  Δt := @clock/tick * 0.0 + 0.002

  ☉ := [ 0,
